`renderInvoice` receives `data` from our own job queue as parsed JSON, typed `any`. By contract the producer always sets `currency` to a 3-letter code and `lines` to a non-empty array. Make `renderInvoice` robust.

```ts
function renderInvoice(data: any): string {
  const total = data.lines.reduce((sum: number, line: any) => sum + line.amount, 0);
  return total.toFixed(2) + ' ' + data.currency;
}
```

